WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:26.760
&gt;&gt; The main facts and figures on this topic
-- an important topic for us, I think -- are

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.900
all in the paper, and I am not going to run
through the paper in order, as it were.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:34.820
I want to focus on the implications of it
for us as we go forward.

00:00:34.820 --> 00:00:39.890
It links very much back to the earlier discussion
about how we make all this practical and concrete

00:00:39.890 --> 00:00:44.030
and get on with doing it.

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:48.540
There is of course the welcome confirmation
that another year of headline preservation

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:55.280
of the health spend, in real terms, is there,
unlike most of the rest of the public sector,

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:58.730
and there are some very graphic charts that
we all saw about that.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:05.899
The big news in this, as David mentioned earlier,
is the creation of the integration transformation

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:15.180
fund of nearly £4 billion that is being put
together.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:21.710
There is £1.7 billion of that which is already
in the system, where health is in one form

00:01:21.710 --> 00:01:26.850
or another supporting the social care system
in its various activities.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:32.190
However, there is an additional £2.1 billion
-- a little bit next year and then a lot of

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:37.500
'15/'16 -- which needs to be found from existing
sources through savings to make that fund

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.670
a reality.

00:01:38.670 --> 00:01:44.730
And it is that which will concentrate our
minds, I think, as we go forward.

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:50.610
We talked about clarity in a large part of
the rest of the agenda.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:54.369
The details of exactly how this fund is going
to work, what the basis of it is going to

00:01:54.369 --> 00:01:58.990
be, which section it is all going to be organised
under is still very much being worked through,

00:01:58.990 --> 00:02:07.210
in detail, between the two departments concerned:
NHS England and the Local Government Association.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:11.850
Contrary to the simplistic assumption in this
paper, which was right at the time we wrote

00:02:11.850 --> 00:02:17.420
it but seems now to be not quite as clear,
it is not a foregone conclusion that the money

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:21.390
will simply go straight across and be held
by the local authority.

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:23.780
It is much more open than that.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:27.410
The one clear thing is that it will be pooled
money which needs to be managed within the

00:02:27.410 --> 00:02:33.834
local health economy by the CCGs, the local
authorities concerned and, indeed, the Health

00:02:33.834 --> 00:02:38.120
and Wellbeing Board as the unit that brings
all that together.

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:42.630
There is now, I think, a shared determination
that the routing of the funding should be

00:02:42.630 --> 00:02:43.709
through the CCGs.

00:02:43.709 --> 00:02:47.750
That is not an administrative matter, that
is quite an important part of making sure

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:53.410
the ownership of this and the ability to influence
the way in which the money is spent and the

00:02:53.410 --> 00:03:03.820
outcomes reflects the locus of the CCG as
the local representation of clinical leadership

00:03:03.820 --> 00:03:06.109
in the health service.

00:03:06.109 --> 00:03:07.400
That is important.

00:03:07.400 --> 00:03:12.570
I would say, though, that until we get complete
crystal clarity on how the mechanism of this

00:03:12.570 --> 00:03:17.139
is going to go, the precise answer to how
the accountabilities get exercised in all

00:03:17.139 --> 00:03:21.970
of this, who exactly is responsible for what,
what the line of sight is through the system

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:26.630
will remain to be clarified.

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:30.860
Whatever the legal niceties, the one thing
we do know is that there are two salient questions

00:03:30.860 --> 00:03:34.010
that we need to address with some urgency.

00:03:34.010 --> 00:03:39.020
The first of those is: what are we going to
do with a fund of £3.8 billion which will

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:42.090
really make a difference in local health economies?

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:47.190
How are we going to get this integration concept
moving for the maximum benefit for patients

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:52.650
and, dare I say it, also for the maximum efficiency
for the taxpayer; both of those go hand in

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:53.650
hand.

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:57.959
It is a really serious piece of work to make
concrete what we have been thinking and talking

00:03:57.959 --> 00:04:02.209
about for many months, if not years.

00:04:02.209 --> 00:04:05.500
Some of that thinking is represented in the
conditions that you can see listed in the

00:04:05.500 --> 00:04:11.609
document in front of you, which are things
that, together, the CCGs and the local authorities

00:04:11.609 --> 00:04:13.329
will have to work their way through.

00:04:13.329 --> 00:04:17.760
However, these will be a deeply local set
of approaches to it that reflect the local

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:19.050
circumstances.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.949
There is not a one-size-fits-all approach.

00:04:20.949 --> 00:04:24.300
That is one of the questions that needs to
be answered, and it is the one frankly that

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.060
most people are perhaps most focused on at
the moment.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:31.080
Equally important, if not more important,
though, is that you cannot spend money that

00:04:31.080 --> 00:04:32.080
you do not have.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:37.139
There is a rather thornier question that we
need to address, which is, how do we generate

00:04:37.139 --> 00:04:42.430
savings of £2 billion on top of all the savings
we already have to generate on an annual basis

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:43.560
to keep going.

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:50.050
How do we generate that in a way which sustains
healthcare and does not cause unintended consequences

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:51.150
of a significant nature.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:54.861
So you will be aware of the kind of efficiency
level in the system at the moment, the ask

00:04:54.861 --> 00:04:59.750
on the system is about 4% to 5% if you add
together the provider and the commissioner

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:01.430
ask at the moment.

00:05:01.430 --> 00:05:06.460
That trips up to at least 6% to 7% when you
put an additional ask of £2 billion into

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:09.879
the system and, as David has already said,
that is a non-trivial ask; it is not just

00:05:09.879 --> 00:05:13.789
a small adjustment to the percentage savings
that need to be done.

00:05:13.789 --> 00:05:26.879
That takes us into a whole different category
of the stretch that is required.

00:05:26.879 --> 00:05:31.520
The most obvious conclusion is that you cannot
achieve that through business as usual; you

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:36.030
cannot do that by salami-slicing; you cannot
do that through incremental gains of one sort

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:39.580
or another.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:43.729
If you want to invest cash, you have to generate
it and that means effectively disinvesting

00:05:43.729 --> 00:05:47.600
in other activities of one sort or another.

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:51.180
In the discussion that we have, we cannot
pretend we can just generate the money without

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:52.490
making changes.

00:05:52.490 --> 00:06:01.210
So we are going to have to find some clear
strategies for shifting activities, shifting

00:06:01.210 --> 00:06:04.620
resource to create that capacity.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:08.930
Equally important, having shifted the activity,
we have to find a way of taking out the cost

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:12.500
from where it is currently being incurred,
and there are complexities in that that we

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.010
are all familiar with.

00:06:14.010 --> 00:06:17.550
The second thing that is obvious is that if
we start planning for that when we get to

00:06:17.550 --> 00:06:22.849
'15/'16, it will be too late to do that because
you cannot do that sort of change on a short-term

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:23.849
basis.

00:06:23.849 --> 00:06:27.400
We have to start planning now if we are going
to free that up for '15/'16.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:30.889
Of course, there is a strong link to the Call
to Action that we talked about earlier.

00:06:30.889 --> 00:06:34.250
This is one of the means by which all of that
gets made concrete.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:38.820
We talked about the Call to Action as being
a five- to ten-year challenge, possibly longer

00:06:38.820 --> 00:06:41.349
than that, in its vision.

00:06:41.349 --> 00:06:45.340
This brings it very much to a 90-week challenge,
and I think we just have to square up to that

00:06:45.340 --> 00:06:48.560
quite quickly and work out how we are going
to make a reality of that.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:50.849
What are we going to do about it?

00:06:50.849 --> 00:06:55.360
To make sure that every health economy is
well prepared for that challenge, we are about

00:06:55.360 --> 00:07:01.389
to launch a process of accelerated planning,
where CCG teams, area teams and other local

00:07:01.389 --> 00:07:06.520
partners in health and social care can work
together to produce strategic plans that address

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:12.971
all of that for the next five years but, crucially,
some two-year operating plans: a bit of a

00:07:12.971 --> 00:07:14.680
novelty for all of us.

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:18.499
These two-year operating plans will make very
concrete, what are the steps we are going

00:07:18.499 --> 00:07:24.550
to do in '14/'15 and '15/'16 to make it real
in that short timeframe that we have?

00:07:24.550 --> 00:07:28.970
They need to be deeply practical plans, and
they need to show in some detail how the various

00:07:28.970 --> 00:07:33.509
parties to that, wherever they sit in the
local health economy, are going to contribute

00:07:33.509 --> 00:07:34.699
to it.

00:07:34.699 --> 00:07:40.199
One of the things we can do to help with that
process is to give some clarity about funding

00:07:40.199 --> 00:07:44.439
for individual organisations for that two-year
period, because you frankly cannot do two-year

00:07:44.439 --> 00:07:47.659
operating plans without clarity of resource.

00:07:47.659 --> 00:07:51.919
One of the benefits of the '15/'16 spending
review being there already -- and we know

00:07:51.919 --> 00:07:56.669
already about '14/'15 -- is that we will know
by the time we get deeply into that planning

00:07:56.669 --> 00:08:01.270
process how much money we have, and we can
make allocations, subject to the Board agreeing

00:08:01.270 --> 00:08:06.000
that when we come to make the formal decisions,
on a two-year basis, to give people the clarity

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:07.580
to plan by.

00:08:07.580 --> 00:08:12.249
We are going to put in place a programme of
support to commissioners to do this planning,

00:08:12.249 --> 00:08:16.160
because it is very clear that this goes beyond
what most health organisations have been able

00:08:16.160 --> 00:08:17.550
to do in the past.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:22.300
We will all be aware from the authorisation
process that the one set of criteria that

00:08:22.300 --> 00:08:29.360
was most frequently a challenge for CCGs has
been the planning set of challenges and, therefore,

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:35.450
putting an additional complexity and length,
as it were, and challenge into the planning

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:39.120
process, we need to put some support in place
to do that.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:49.600
As 
you would expect, we are doing this in partnership

00:08:49.600 --> 00:08:54.290
with the Commissioning Assembly, which of
course is our link between NHS England and

00:08:54.290 --> 00:08:59.170
the CCGs, to make these things happen in a
joined-up fashion, and we have started that

00:08:59.170 --> 00:09:01.970
dialogue already, with Ros's support and help.

00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:06.880
We are also in discussion right now with the
Local Government Association and with a variety

00:09:06.880 --> 00:09:11.320
of arm's-length Bodies, the national partners
that we have -- whether that be the Trust

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:15.750
Development Authority, whether it be Monitor
-- to see how we can make this a truly integrated

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:16.750
piece of planning.

00:09:16.750 --> 00:09:20.660
If we do it on a pure commissioning basis,
you cannot answer half of those questions

00:09:20.660 --> 00:09:21.660
that I posed at the beginning.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:24.930
It is really, really important that we have
it joined up, and I think there are some good

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:29.610
signs at the moment from the early conversations
that David has had with anyone else who is

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:35.529
called David in the country, and the follow-up
conversations that we are having with people

00:09:35.529 --> 00:09:40.310
who are not called David, just how we might
bring all of that process together into an

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:41.310
integrated thing.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:46.670
It is the only way we will make it stick.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:50.959
There is one additional complication, which
is put into paragraph 10, in that, at the

00:09:50.959 --> 00:09:54.440
same time as delivering all of that, we will
have to make some very substantial savings

00:09:54.440 --> 00:10:00.600
in our admin costs, coming on top of the reductions
of 30% to 50% that we have already absorbed

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:04.350
in putting this organisation together, and
where we are already trying to make sure that

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:08.420
we have that resource in the right place,
in the right measure, and able to tackle the

00:10:08.420 --> 00:10:09.420
challenge.

00:10:09.420 --> 00:10:14.530
If you take those two things together, two-year
planning with an enormous ask in '15/'16,

00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:18.589
and the need to think about what we do with
our admin structures, it is a massive test

00:10:18.589 --> 00:10:22.209
for a commissioning system that, as David
has already said, has only been in existence

00:10:22.209 --> 00:10:24.550
for a matter of weeks.

00:10:24.550 --> 00:10:27.470
We do not have very long to put these plans
together, because we need to start implementing

00:10:27.470 --> 00:10:28.470
them soon.

00:10:28.470 --> 00:10:34.790
I do think that if we tackle this with a real
passion, determination and support for each

00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:38.870
other, it will give a real impetus to the
kind of transformation that we have talked

00:10:38.870 --> 00:10:40.080
about in the Call to Action.

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:44.399
It will end up being a positive thing, albeit
a challenging thing.

00:10:44.399 --> 00:10:49.960
That is what I wanted to say by way of introduction.

00:10:49.960 --> 00:11:06.110
I would be keen to get any thoughts and help
that people around the table can bring to

00:11:06.110 --> 00:11:07.540
bear.

00:11:07.540 --> 00:11:20.480
&gt;&gt; Thanks to the Paul for that very clear
setting out of the enormity of the challenge,

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:23.290
which I fully accept.

00:11:23.290 --> 00:11:28.710
However, I would want to pay tribute, in a
sense, to the recognition that this gives

00:11:28.710 --> 00:11:34.670
to the importance of social care in the system,
and putting money where your mouth is, is

00:11:34.670 --> 00:11:43.720
a very important signal, and I welcome greatly
the stretch in social care that we all need,

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:49.949
as I say.

00:11:49.949 --> 00:12:00.540
The impact of cuts in local government is
not evenly spread, and there is a risk, in

00:12:00.540 --> 00:12:03.250
a sense.

00:12:03.250 --> 00:12:07.600
It is not a straightforward replacement for
cuts; that is obviously not what is intended,

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:12.970
but there will be places that are definitely
having more of an impact than others, and

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:19.740
how our distribution mechanism will assist
or, in fact, potentially not recognise that,

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:21.899
I am interested in you thoughts on that.

00:12:21.899 --> 00:12:26.720
&gt;&gt; There is a precedent question, which comes
back to how we are going to do all of this

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:30.589
stuff, which is, who gets to decide the distribution
of this?

00:12:30.589 --> 00:12:33.290
That is one of the questions that we are currently
working through.

00:12:33.290 --> 00:12:37.709
It will be no surprise to you, I guess, to
recognise that we think it would be a good

00:12:37.709 --> 00:12:40.500
idea if we did that particular exercise.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:44.740
That is not the case with the current social
care transfer that we are required to make,

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:48.579
but I do think it would be important for us
to do that as part of the allocation discussion,

00:12:48.579 --> 00:12:52.319
more broadly, because we need to make sure
the total funds get to the right places in

00:12:52.319 --> 00:12:56.800
the right measure, and we can only do that
if we bring together the various strands.

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:59.860
That is my aspiration, Moira.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:03.630
I think it is really quite important that
that is the way it gets transacted.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:12.019
As we speak, I would not say that is in the
bag yet.

00:13:12.019 --> 00:13:19.699
&gt;&gt; Paul raised the point that I think is critical,
and I think we as a Board must wait to see

00:13:19.699 --> 00:13:20.699
where it comes back.

00:13:20.699 --> 00:13:29.050
However, I am a simple soul, and accountability
has to follow, whether you are responsible

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:33.920
for deciding on where the money is spent and
how it is spent, and the outcomes from it.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:40.470
I will be very keen to make sure that we can
see that absolutely direct line of accountability

00:13:40.470 --> 00:13:48.009
to spend on outcomes, and if we are not having
that as a Board of NHS England, then I struggle

00:13:48.009 --> 00:13:51.570
to see how we can then be accountable for
the spend.

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:55.829
That is a point that you would expect me to
make.

00:13:55.829 --> 00:14:06.579
&gt;&gt; I think in principle putting the money
behind driving outcomes based in the community

00:14:06.579 --> 00:14:09.670
is our direction of travel and has to be a
really, really good thing to do.

00:14:09.670 --> 00:14:15.629
I like that, and if accepting the enormity
of it drives us in the direction we need to

00:14:15.629 --> 00:14:20.480
do, we need to understand the implications
of that.

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:24.490
We need to start acting now; this is not something
we start in 2015 or '16.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:28.060
It is going to afford some real change very
quickly.

00:14:28.060 --> 00:14:32.519
I am almost more worried about the admin bit,
because it is taking more capacity out of

00:14:32.519 --> 00:14:33.519
the system.

00:14:33.519 --> 00:14:39.449
It is taking the capacity to take the capacity
out of the system, the brainpower of the Exec

00:14:39.449 --> 00:14:46.529
in particular, at a time when we are trying
to not only establish where we are, but accelerate

00:14:46.529 --> 00:14:47.690
it.

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:53.449
This is accelerating the changes we need to
do, and I would love to know what risk assessment

00:14:53.449 --> 00:14:59.620
-- dare I use the words -- has been put in
place, and just to think that through.

00:14:59.620 --> 00:15:01.681
Directionally, I love it; I think it is great.

00:15:01.681 --> 00:15:02.681
It is a really good thing.

00:15:02.681 --> 00:15:07.319
It will empower Health and Wellbeing Boards,
it will get people playing nicely together

00:15:07.319 --> 00:15:09.170
across the country.

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:13.810
If we do it at the same time as getting rid
of all the people who can actually deliver

00:15:13.810 --> 00:15:16.631
it, it probably will not be quite so good.

00:15:16.631 --> 00:15:23.370
&gt;&gt; I think that is a really good point, and
I think we should ask for transparency from

00:15:23.370 --> 00:15:27.970
the department about what the risk assessment
was on the admin cost, so we can look at it

00:15:27.970 --> 00:15:34.550
and test it ourselves to see how that is,
as well as the conclusions they made about

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:36.830
the £3.8 billion.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:46.000
Just to reinforce the point that Paul makes,
this £2 billion is on top of the £4 billion

00:15:46.000 --> 00:15:48.790
we already have to save.

00:15:48.790 --> 00:15:51.750
You cannot focus on the £2 billion alone;
you have to do the whole thing.

00:15:51.750 --> 00:15:59.050
In some of the conversations I have heard,
people have missed that point, which I think

00:15:59.050 --> 00:16:03.110
is a really important points, because it is
not that we have £2 billion sitting around

00:16:03.110 --> 00:16:06.660
somewhere doing nothing, it is tied up in
services.

00:16:06.660 --> 00:16:07.880
The way in which we tackle that is going to
be really important.

00:16:07.880 --> 00:16:11.730
That is the first thing, just to reinforce
how big this is.

00:16:11.730 --> 00:16:16.540
The second thing is, I am slightly worried
that what will happen is we will get involved

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:23.500
in a long and detailed conversation about
the technical ways the money flows in the

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:28.639
system, when actually, the real issue is how
we redesign the services.

00:16:28.639 --> 00:16:35.189
In any planning system that we have, we need
to make sure that that is forefront in everybody's

00:16:35.189 --> 00:16:39.629
minds, how we are going to redesign the system.

00:16:39.629 --> 00:16:42.560
We have to do the technical things, that is
absolutely right, but I just think I can see

00:16:42.560 --> 00:16:46.519
exactly where people will go in all that.

00:16:46.519 --> 00:16:51.339
I think there needs to be a real transparency,
openness and honesty with the public about

00:16:51.339 --> 00:16:53.980
what this means practically.

00:16:53.980 --> 00:17:00.449
That is why, in a sense, it reinforces the
whole issue of the Call to Action.

00:17:00.449 --> 00:17:07.020
Had we not done it, we would have had to have
done it now, I think.

00:17:07.020 --> 00:17:11.020
It seems that that is really important as
far as we are concerned.

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:20.220
&gt;&gt; I am just going to echo what has been by
David, which is that I go immediately for

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:25.920
the implications for what happens on the ground
in communities.

00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:33.890
I guess it drives everything to a point of,
how do we in a sense sign of the process of

00:17:33.890 --> 00:17:37.470
service redesign around individuals and communities?

00:17:37.470 --> 00:17:44.140
If we do not get that right, we will end up
either fighting about who owns which bit of

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:48.780
the budget, or salami-slicing, neither of
which will work.

00:17:48.780 --> 00:17:55.610
For me, the implications are about commissioning,
actually, and the way it drives into the system

00:17:55.610 --> 00:18:00.340
processes for understanding what people have,
what they do not have, what they need, and

00:18:00.340 --> 00:18:04.850
how we will redesign the services to deliver
it and how we involve them in doing that.

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:12.151
We are not starting with a huge amount of
technical know-how; there is some, but it

00:18:12.151 --> 00:18:17.500
is not something we have done, so there is
a rapid learning curve as to how we do that

00:18:17.500 --> 00:18:19.650
and how we get the sign-offs all the way up
the line.

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:27.140
I have to say it would be in error to paint
a rosy picture of understanding between health

00:18:27.140 --> 00:18:29.720
and social care throughout the country.

00:18:29.720 --> 00:18:33.840
What this is fundamentally about is power,
and what this forces -- whether we like it

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:40.270
or not -- is a transfer of power, which is
not something we have done systemically, effectively,

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:41.640
efficiently, in the past.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:48.100
It is a really serious shift; it is almost
a paradigm shift forced by the money.

00:18:48.100 --> 00:18:52.660
The other point I wanted to make was that
I am very worried about the implications of

00:18:52.660 --> 00:18:55.150
the £300 million.

00:18:55.150 --> 00:18:58.500
While it is really important we look at the
frontline and all that, I am really keen to

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:03.130
know what the implications of the £300 million
are on us almost before we start doing the

00:19:03.130 --> 00:19:07.500
other bit, so we have a clear understanding
of what we can do and what we cannot in the

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.110
fixed period of time.

00:19:10.110 --> 00:19:16.660
&gt;&gt; Quite blatantly, the aim of this money
rightly and properly is to support those people

00:19:16.660 --> 00:19:20.970
who do not need to be in hospital to stay
at home and to get people who are in hospital

00:19:20.970 --> 00:19:23.440
and are ready to go home, home more quickly.

00:19:23.440 --> 00:19:28.480
We know from the work we do out and about
in the country that actually, whilst often

00:19:28.480 --> 00:19:33.400
this is a social care issue, it can almost
equally often be a health services issue in

00:19:33.400 --> 00:19:36.710
that the right community services are not
in place, the right primary care services

00:19:36.710 --> 00:19:37.800
are not in place.

00:19:37.800 --> 00:19:42.960
I do hope as we move through that the way
that this money can be used and the way it

00:19:42.960 --> 00:19:48.540
is looked at on the ground is that people
remember that it is sometimes NHS services

00:19:48.540 --> 00:19:52.570
that are needed to support these individuals,
not just social care ones.

00:19:52.570 --> 00:20:03.310
&gt;&gt; I just want to report that we have had
very positive discussions so far with Local

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:05.380
Government Association about this.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:13.430
I guess you might not find that surprising
given the potential investment that local

00:20:13.430 --> 00:20:14.950
government can share in from this.

00:20:14.950 --> 00:20:24.880
I think they have been a very honest and serious
set of discussions where local governments

00:20:24.880 --> 00:20:30.830
-- not just the officials, but some of the
political infrastructure around Local Government

00:20:30.830 --> 00:20:40.560
Association -- have recognised that this is
not a financial transaction, but that it is

00:20:40.560 --> 00:20:49.340
a really significant step towards a shared
responsibility, not just to design services

00:20:49.340 --> 00:20:57.710
differently that will better serve local populations,
but then to back that up not just with the

00:20:57.710 --> 00:21:04.360
investment, but with the political support
that will be needed to bring about some really

00:21:04.360 --> 00:21:06.290
quite challenging changes.

00:21:06.290 --> 00:21:10.830
They will be in the interest of patients in
the community, but they will be challenging

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:13.450
service changes.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:22.100
The potential game changer here is this money
draws together NHS leadership and political

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:28.430
leadership in local government to support
those changes, whereas, at times in the past,

00:21:28.430 --> 00:21:36.180
I think it is fair to say local government
has felt able to step back and just criticise.

00:21:36.180 --> 00:21:43.650
I am very hopeful from those discussions that
this could be a step into a significantly

00:21:43.650 --> 00:21:46.720
different quality of collaboration.

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:51.180
&gt;&gt; I think some really telling points have
been made in that discussion.

00:21:51.180 --> 00:21:55.100
Paul, is there anything else that you would
like to come back on, on what you have heard

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:56.100
from us?

00:21:56.100 --> 00:21:57.100
&gt;&gt; I do not think so.

00:21:57.100 --> 00:22:00.720
I have obviously taken note of the sentiment
of the Board, if I can put it that way, and

00:22:00.720 --> 00:22:02.650
will make sure that gets worked into the programme.

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:06.809
I have taken onboard in particular the admin
comments, which clearly we will pick up.

00:22:06.809 --> 00:22:12.570
&gt;&gt; Thanks for that; and actually, frankly,
the capacity issue is I think just quite scary,

00:22:12.570 --> 00:22:17.590
hanging over all of us on top of everything
else that we are doing.

